1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,872
The missing voice arrived in a lecture hall, from a member of the cleaning staff.

2
00:00:04,872 --> 00:00:13,007
She had worked in the same building for eleven years, and she had never been asked what she thought of the academy.

3
00:00:13,007 --> 00:00:17,842
“You teach the students how to read a page,” she said.

4
00:00:17,842 --> 00:00:31,151
“Nobody teaches them how to read a person.” The revelation spread through the room faster than the information, and along the back wall the class stopped taking notes.

5
00:00:31,151 --> 00:00:34,186
Her own schooling had ended early.

6
00:00:34,186 --> 00:00:43,061
She had learned medicine from her mother, literature from the radio, and the art of remembering from a small notebook.

7
00:00:43,061 --> 00:00:48,820
“I possess no diploma,” she said, “and I am not ignorant.

8
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:58,145
I am a learner.” She was literate in three languages, and her enlightenment had come from work rather than from a lecture.

9
00:00:58,145 --> 00:01:02,450
Not one word of it had been written down until that hour.

10
00:01:02,450 --> 00:01:09,454
The writer who took notes for the student paper called her a scholar by the end of the hour.

11
00:01:09,454 --> 00:01:17,809
The educational review changed shape: for one week, the staff would teach and the students would listen.

12
00:01:17,809 --> 00:01:25,414
The first session was on the foundation of a good question; the second was on the discipline of silence.

13
00:01:25,414 --> 00:01:32,699
“Skill is not the same as education,” the cleaner said, and both of them wrote it down.

14
00:01:32,699 --> 00:01:40,248
Experience, she added, is not transferred by a lecture but by work.

15
00:01:40,248 --> 00:01:44,118
Circulation of the reading-room books doubled.

16
00:01:44,118 --> 00:01:54,078
A zoological exhibit in the hall was visited by a class that had never entered it, and a bright exhibition of student writing hung beside it.

17
00:01:54,078 --> 00:02:01,962
The examination results, usually the only measure the school published, looked suddenly thin.

18
00:02:01,962 --> 00:02:08,477
Such a result had never appeared in any report the academy had produced.

19
00:02:08,477 --> 00:02:14,342
He wrote a review of the week, and she read it aloud at the fellowship meeting.

20
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:38,446
“If we generalize from one cleaner,” the learned professor said, “we learn nothing.” “If we do not,” Maya answered, “we learn less.” His own study of the reading room had used a different method, and he often said so; toward the end of the week he began to research the language of the staff's own example.

21
00:02:38,446 --> 00:02:43,466
The learner had taught the academy something that no exam could hold.

22
00:02:43,466 --> 00:02:53,090
The first reader of the transcript was a second-year student, and the week had done more to educate the faculty than three years of the map.

23
00:02:53,090 --> 00:03:01,564
The faculty would now have to seek a second opinion, and the staff were happy to provide one.
